NEARS-2198 QA (2026-08-16, emulator-5556) — PRE-EXISTING, not introduced by this change.

RouteHelper.getPaymentRoute interpolates subscriptionUrl / addFundUrl RAW (unencoded)
into its own query string (UserApp/lib/helper/route_helper.dart §getPaymentRoute):

  '$payment?id=$id&...&add-fund-url=$addFundUrl&...&subscription-url=$subscriptionUrl
   &store_id=$storeId&create_account=$createAccount&create_user_id=$createUserId
   &group_id=$groupId&payment_token=$paymentToken'

So any '&' inside the injected URL terminates the `subscription-url` value and the
remainder is re-parsed as sibling route parameters.

MEASURED (relay log, initial redirect_link delivered via the route):
  injected : http://10.0.2.2:8001/subscription-success?flag=fail&&token=eyJvcmRlciI6IjkxMTA4In0=
  fetched  : GET /subscription-success?flag=fail                      <-- truncated at the first '&'

  injected : http://10.0.2.2:8001/subscription-success?token=eyJvcmRlciI6IjkxMTA4In0=&&flag=success
  fetched  : GET /subscription-success?token=eyJvcmRlciI6IjkxMTA4In0= <-- flag lost entirely

Impact on THIS ticket: none. Production delivers the callback as an in-webview redirect
from Processor.php §payment_response, which never passes through getPaymentRoute — verified
live by re-running every case through a gateway 302, where onLoadStart received the full
'?flag=..&&token=..' URL and every AC passed.

Latent risk (why it is still worth a ticket): the parameters that FOLLOW the url in the
route string — store_id, create_account, create_user_id, group_id (NEARS-1291),
payment_token (NEARS-1301) — can be clobbered by a same-named query parameter carried
inside the injected URL. Fix shape: Uri.encodeComponent() the url values.
